        'A project runs along a route: five stages that follow each other. Intake: what is the problem and is it worth solving? Plan: what do we do, when, with whom? Run: do the work and steer it. Land: make the change work for the people who live with it. Close: prove the result and hand over.\n\nThe stages are not boxes to tick but questions you answer in order.',
        'Each stage leaves behind one thing the next stage needs: a stage product. Intake delivers an agreed problem and a project mandate document. Plan delivers a plan with a baseline to measure against later. Run delivers a working rhythm of status and decisions. Land delivers a handover. Close delivers a closing decision with proven results.\n\nIf a stage product is missing, the next stage stands on loose ground.',
